<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gelon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 540–478 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a> · Also known as Gelon of Syracuse</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gelon was tyrant of Gela from about 491 BCE and of Syracuse from 485 BCE. He moved his capital to Syracuse, enlarging it with transplanted populations, and made it the strongest Greek city in the west. With <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theron-of-acragas">Theron of Acragas</a> he crushed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthaginians</a> at the Battle of Himera in 480 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gelon.jpg" alt="Gelon" width="320" height="402" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Max Karl Baldamus · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gelone_(Ritratto).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
